to lock in your decision? Click the link below to pay your deposit now! Deposit Today We use cookies on this site to enhance your user experience. By selecting the Accept button, you agree to us doing so. Accept Pay Your Deposit First-Years & Transfers - Pay Deposit Now International Students - Pay Deposit Now Event Survey We're thrilled that you've decided to attend North Central College! Make your $100 tuition deposit to officially reserve your place in the class. If you plan to live on campus, please also submit your $100 room deposit to save your space in the residence halls.* We accept deposits electronically at the link above, over the phone at 630-637-5800, by check made to North Central College or in person by visiting the Admission Welcome Center. Please note, all deposits are non-refundable. *We're committed to providing access to enrollment at North Central to all admitted students and offer tuition deposit waivers when payment presents a financial hardship. Please contact your admission counselor to learn more about the waiver program if you are currently facing a financial situation that could otherwise prevent you from enrolling at the College. Please note, only tuition deposits can be waived. Admitted First-Years Now that you're officially a Cardinal, there may be a few other items to check off your list in preparation for your start at North Central. Check out the Admitted Student page for incoming first-years to view important next steps in your transition to college. Learn more Admitted Transfers Congratulations on making your transfer decision! As a next step, you may want to check out the Admitted Student page for transfer students, as it includes a number of helpful resources to assist in making your transition to our campus as smooth as possible. Learn more Admitted International Students Welcome to North Central! To prepare you for your transition to campus, there are a few additional steps you'll need to take. Learn about visas, airport pick-up, Orientation and more! Learn more Housing Living on campus? Complete your online roommate questionnaire after submitting your deposits. You'll need your North Central login credentials, which you can find in your acceptance packet. Find a roommate Questions? Our staff in the Office of Admission has answers! We look forward to officially welcoming you to campus! Should you have additional questions regarding the deposit or next steps, please contact us. Phone: 630-637-5800 Email: admissions@noctrl.edu Admission Welcome Center is located on 30 N. Brainard Street, Naperville, Illinois 60540 in Old Main on the 1st Floor. Locate Old Main on the campus map under Building 10. Apply Request Information Donate Admissions Academic Programs Online Store About The College Work Here Athletics Fine Arts Alumni Hire Our Students Rent Our Facilities Report Misconduct IBHE Complaint System North Central College 30 N. Brainard Street Naperville, IL 60540 Campus Directory Mission Statement Privacy Policy & Legal Notice © 2026 North Central College Back to top"
    },
    "https://www.northcentralcollege.edu/career-development": {
      "title": "Eyebrow Menu",
      "description": "Center for Career and Professional Development | North Central College Skip to main content Eyebrow Menu Visit Apply Programs Athletics Resources for Students Parents School Counselors Media Faculty & Staff Prospective Employees Search × View full results < Back Main Menu Home Apply Visit Give Academics Academics Programs Undergraduate Graduate Colleges & Schools Honors Program Cardinal Directions Study Abroad Shimer Great Books School Resources Academic Affairs Center for Student Success Course Catalog Library First Generation Programs Admissions Admissions Applicant Information Prospective Students Admitted Students Former Students Admission Events First-Year & Transfer Events Fine Arts Auditions Virtual Tour Admission Counselors First-Year Admission Counselors Transfer Admission Counselors International Admission Counselors Graduate Admission Counselors Application Resources Pay Your Deposit Community College Partnerships First-Generation College Students Veterans Reserve Officers Training Corps (ROTC) Non-Degree Applicants Undocumented Applicants Student Experience Student Experience Student Life Explore Housing Commuter Life Campus Dining Student Engagement and Belonging Center for Social Impact Faith & Action Activities Clubs & Activities Athletics Recreation & Fitness Living in Naperville Visit Chicago Reserve Officers Training Corps (ROTC) Campus Resources Student Affairs Center for Career and Professional Development Wellness Student Disability Services Title IX International Student Services First-Generation Program Campus Safety Tuition & Aid Tuition and Aid Tuition and Aid Undergraduate Cost of Attendance Graduate Cost of Attendance Grants for Undergraduates Scholarship Opportunities The College The College About Us Leadership Trustees Strategic Plan Community Values Transparency Sustainability Institutional Advancement Corporate Engagement Utility Menu Calendar Athletics Fine Arts Faculty & Staff Newsroom Search Pay Your Deposit Have you been admitted and need to lock in your decision? Click the link below to pay your deposit now! Deposit Today We use cookies on this site to enhance your user experience. By selecting the Accept button, you agree to us doing so. Accept Center for Career and Professional Development Contact Us Join Handshake Hub Resources Welcome! The Center for Career and Professional Development (CCPD) assists students of all majors with identifying interests and career goals and creating meaningful opportunities to help you succeed in your academic, personal, and professional goals. The CCPD is dedicated to supporting and empowering students in their exploration, preparation, and pursuit of their chosen career journey. For employers looking to recruit North Central talent, check out our hire our students page . Connect with Employers on Handshake Handshake is our online platform to help you find a meaningful career. Everything you need to connect with Center for Career and Professional Development is on Handshake! Schedule appointments, download career resources, view upcoming events and more! Visit Handshake to update your profile and see who is looking for NCC interns and employees. Join Handshake How the center for career and professional development supports students Individual One-on-One Appointments Students can meet with the CCPD team to discuss a variety of topics. Some of the most popular topics students seek support on are: Career Exploration: Explore who you are, your goals, and what matters to you Internship & Job Search: Create personalized internship and job search plans Internship Approvals: Receive internship approval and support while on internship Networking: Expand networking skills & connections with employers Internship & Job Application: Review job search materials - resumes, cover letters, applications Interview Preparation: Engage with mock interviews to gain confidence Schedule an Appointment Drop-In Center Meet with a Career Peer Advisor Students may access the Drop-In Center in Oesterle Library #114. The CCPD Drop-In Center is open from 12 - 4pm on Tuesdays, Wednesdays, and Thursdays during the academic year. North Central College Career Peer Advisors support students by answering questions and providing guidance on the following topics: Resume and cover letter reviews Introductions to the CCPD career resources and events 15 minute career conversations about career exploration Guidance on internship and/or job search strategy Handshake and LinkedIn support Preparation for career events by practicing your elevator pitch and researching employers Visit Us Career Events & Fairs North Central College Job & Internship Fair (September) CareerFest (February) Appointments Events Jobs & Internships Resources Cardinal Career Closet Whether you have an upcoming interview or you're starting a new internship or job, we've got the perfect outfit for you! The Cardinal Career Closet is open to all North Central students. The Cardinal Career Closet Mission is to increase access to quality professional attire to students for career-related experiences, interviews, and professional networking events. CCPD Resources Build Your Resume, Cover Letter, and Other Career Documents Explore a wide range of career resources designed to help you confidently navigate your career journey. From resumes and cover letters to interviewing, networking, job and internship searching, graduate school planning, and professional branding, you'll find practical tools and expert guidance to help you achieve your goals. Our Career Peer Advisors and professional staff are available to provide personalized support whenever you need it. Career Resources All College Career Readiness Requirement At North Central, we want students to find a postgraduate path—a job, graduate school, service—that is meaningful for them. And we want them to be confident that they are being prepared to succeed on the path they choose. The All College Career Readiness Requirement allows students to explore their strengths and the postgraduate options available to them; develop a story and materials to share with employers and graduate school committees to translate their North Central experiences in exciting ways; and to practice what they’ve learned in the classroom in internship, undergraduate research, practica, and other field experience settings. Learn More Prepare for Interviews The CCPD team is dedicated to helping students prepare for various interview experiences. Students can schedule one-on-one appointments for mock interviews, attend interview workshops, or use the robust interview platform, Big Interview. With Big Interview, students can gain valuable feedback on their interviewing skills and build confidence to excel in their interviews. Big Interview College Career Consortium of Illinois North Central College is a proud member of the College Career Consortium of Illinois (CCCI), a respected consortium of 15 colleges and universities representing more than 50,000 students. As a member institution, North Central students have exclusive access to CareerFest. CareerFest is an opportunity for students to meet with employers from a wide range of industries who are actively recruiting students for internships, part-time positions, and full-time careers. College Career Consortium of Illinois Alumni Career Support We want you to receive the right coaching for where you're at in your career. There are different support options depending on your graduation date. Alumni who graduated from North Central College less than two years ago have access to a variety of career support and resources, including access to: Handshake - North Central's primary career engagement platform for students and alumni to seek internships and full-time roles for entry-level talent. Career events, programs, and workshops, including the annual North Central College Job & Internship Fair. Drop-In Center support (located in Oesterle Library #114). One-on-one appointments with professional staff, both in-person and virtual via Teams. Alumni who graduated from North Central College more than two years ago will be directed to receive support from the Career and Networking Center , an expert group of business professionals who aid job seekers, career changers, and those seeking career advancement. All North Central College alumni will receive a discount on the membership by following the steps below: Navigate to the Career and Networking Center homepage. Select \"Become a Member.\" Select the 3 Month $75 membership option as your choice. Scroll down to the coupon code open box and include the code CNC25 to allow you to receive the $75 three month membership for the discounted rate of $50. Career & Networking Center Become a Career Peer Advisor Do you enjoy helping your peers through education and leadership? Are you looking for an on-campus job opportunity to develop professionally, while helping your peers do the same? If this describes you, consider applying for the Career Peer Advisor (CPA) program. Career Peer Advisors are trained paraprofessionals who provide career assistance through the CCPD Drop-In Center, career events, and programs. Working closely with the CCPD team, CPAs advise/coach their peers on quick career-related concerns, such as the career planning process, effective internship and job search skills, resume and cover letter writing, interviewing strategies, and leveraging online career resources. Learn More Student Employment On Campus Campus employment provides great opportunities for students to advance their career readiness skills.  Students looking for employment opportunities on campus can search for open positions through our Human Resource department. Search Job Openings Questions? Connect with Center for Career and Professional Development Our staff is happy to help and answer any questions you may have. Simply contact us for more information. Contact Us Apply Request Information Donate Admissions Academic Programs Online Store About The College Work Here Athletics Fine Arts Alumni Hire Our Students Rent Our Facilities Report Misconduct IBHE Complaint System North Central College 30 N. Brainard Street Naperville, IL 60540 Campus Directory Mission Statement Privacy Policy & Legal Notice © 2026 North Central College Back to top"
    },
